<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Varkhuman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 650s–660s</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Varkhuman was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> in the mid-7th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> recognised him as ruler of Kangju around 658. He is named in an inscription on the Ambassadors' Painting at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrasiab">Afrasiab</a>, a palace mural that shows envoys from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, the Turks and other peoples arriving at his court, one of the finest surviving works of Sogdian art.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/varkhuman.jpg" alt="Varkhuman" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sogdiana._Samarkand_(Ikhshids)._Varkhuman._Circa_CE_650-675.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
